error[E0041]: cannot store 'K' in interface 'M': only a struct can be the concrete type behind an interface value
  --> check_assert_enum_target.bit:16:17
   |
16 |   let (k, ok) = m.(K)
   |                 ^^^^^ an interface value is the receiver's object pointer, so a non-struct has nothing to point to (§14.3)
